from review import card,save,DATE
i='TCS-3717';_,c=card(i);refs=c['references'];refs[0]['locator']='Section 2.2, unlabeled distribution samples and function-query cost; Theorem 1; Section 4, constant-round poly(k/ε) question.'
refs += [dict(id='full',title='Almost Optimal Distribution-free Junta Testing',authors='Nader H. Bshouty',year=2019,url='https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.00717',pdf_url='https://arxiv.org/pdf/1901.00717',locator='Full preprint; Section 2.2 retains function-query-only cost; Section 4 repeats the constant-round question.'),dict(id='previous',title='Distribution-free Junta Testing',authors='Xi Chen; Zhengyang Liu; Rocco A. Servedio; Ying Sheng; Jinyu Xie',year=2018,url='https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.04859',pdf_url='https://arxiv.org/pdf/1802.04859',locator='STOC 2018, DOI 10.1145/3188745.3188842; full version Definition 2.1 and following paragraph count labeled samples plus membership queries and define nonadaptivity after a labeled-sample phase; Theorem 1.2.')]
issue='The testing promise and desired O(1)-round, poly(k/ε)-query scale are recoverable, but the source does not reconcile its sample and round conventions with the lower bound it cites. Its Section 2.2 supplies unlabeled D samples and counts only queries to f, without a separate sample budget. The cited 2018 model charges labeled samples and membership queries together and calls an algorithm nonadaptive when its membership-query batch may depend on an earlier labeled-sample phase. A complete benchmark must decide whether unlabeled sampling is charged or bounded and whether sample labels contribute an adaptation phase. Imposing a polynomial total-oracle budget or permitting unbounded free samples changes the resource claim; no equivalence or author-supported choice was located.'
notes=['Restored the missing proximity parameter ε and the uniform polynomial-in-k/ε target independent of ambient dimension n.','Defined k-juntas, arbitrary unknown distributions, distance, both oracle types and two-sided success.','Checked the original nonadaptive lower bound and found a material difference in sample accounting and what is called one round.','Preserved the round-complexity question while leaving its exact sampling/round convention uncertified rather than silently imposing a stronger total-oracle budget.']
save(i,dict(formal='Can distribution-free testing of k-juntas be performed in a constant number of adaptive query rounds using poly(k/ε) queries, with constants independent of the ambient dimension n? The tester must accept every k-junta and reject every Boolean function at distance at least ε from all k-juntas under an arbitrary unknown distribution, with success probability at least 2/3 in each case. The source recovers this target but leaves a material sampling convention unresolved: its function-query-only definition differs from the charged labeled-sample model used by its cited one-round lower bound. The completed benchmark must fix that convention before the round/query assertion is certified.',definitions='Let n≥1, 1≤k≤n and ε∈(0,1). A function f:{0,1}ⁿ→{0,1} is a k-junta if some J⊆[n], |J|≤k, and g:{0,1}ᴶ→{0,1} satisfy f(x)=g(x_J) for every x. Let J_{n,k} be the class of all such functions. For a distribution D on {0,1}ⁿ, dist_D(f,J_{n,k})=min_{g∈J_{n,k}}Pr_{X∼D}[f(X)≠g(X)]. The target function and D are fixed before the randomized test. The source supplies a membership oracle returning f(x) on any chosen x and a sample oracle returning a fresh independent X∼D. The tester is given n,k,ε but no explicit description of D. It must accept if f∈J_{n,k}, reject if dist_D(f,J_{n,k})≥ε, and may behave arbitrarily between these cases. Probability is over its random bits and sample-oracle draws. Two-sided error is allowed; the separate one-sided question is not imposed here. In a batch of membership queries, all queried strings are chosen before any values from that batch are revealed; later batches may depend on earlier answers. A constant-round bound requires some fixed integer r independent of n,k,ε,f,D, and poly(k/ε) requires fixed C,b with worst-case charged cost at most C(k/ε)ᵇ. Which calls are charged and whether an initial labeled-sample phase counts toward r must still be fixed. Obtaining a label from the source’s unlabeled oracle requires a membership query. In contrast, the 2018 oracle returns (X,f(X)) directly, charges that sample and permits a nonadaptive membership batch to depend on all initial labeled samples. These conventions are explicitly distinguished; the card does not identify them without a resource-preserving argument. There is no requested bit-operation running-time bound.',question_type='yes_no',answer_criterion='Recover a consistent sample-cost and adaptation-round convention from the source question and its underlying testing model. Then establish or refute existence of fixed r,C,b achieving the displayed tester guarantees uniformly in n,k,ε. Until that convention is fixed, a polynomial bound counting only membership queries and a polynomial bound counting every labeled sample cannot be treated as the same answer. A uniform-distribution tester or a tester with a number of rounds growing with k does not answer the intended distribution-free constant-round question.',context_blocks=[dict(title='The fully adaptive upper bound is almost linear in k',text='Bshouty gives a two-sided adaptive tester using O((k/ε)log(k/ε)) function queries and asks whether a constant number of rounds can retain polynomial dependence on k/ε.',citation='primary'),dict(title='The cited nonadaptive lower bound counts sampled labels',text='The earlier paper proves an Ω(2^{k/3}) lower bound at ε=1/3 for k≤n/200. Its cost includes labeled examples and membership queries, and its nonadaptive batch may depend on the initial labeled examples. That exact statement supplies context; it is not automatically a lower bound with arbitrarily many free distribution samples.',citation='previous'),dict(title='The discrepancy survives in the full preprint',text='The later source’s full version retains unlabeled D sampling, counts only queries to f, and repeats the constant-round question. It does not specify a matching sample budget or a formal round convention.',citation='full'),dict(title='This is distinct from the uniform-distribution question',text='The source separately asks about few-round testing when distance is uniform. Polynomial-query nonadaptive algorithms already exist in that model, whereas this card keeps the arbitrary unknown distribution.',citation='primary')],why='The intended tradeoff asks how much sequential feedback is needed for dimension-independent testing under an unknown distribution, between polynomial adaptive complexity and an exponential nonadaptive lower bound in the charged-sample model.',references=refs,progress=[dict(date='2018',text='Polynomial-query adaptive testing and an exponential nonadaptive lower bound are proved in a model counting labeled samples and membership queries.',citation='previous'),dict(date='2019',text='The almost-linear adaptive upper bound and constant-round question appear; the source counts only function queries.',citation='primary'),dict(date=DATE,text='Review restores the exact promise and ε dependence, but identifies unresolved sample-cost and round conventions across the cited formulations.',citation='full')],status='uncertain',status_note='Read the conference and full versions and the cited lower-bound model. The missing ε is restored, but a fully self-contained round-complexity proposition needs the stated sampling conventions reconciled. Searches through 12 September 2026 did not locate a later resolution or clarification. Recent junta testing for real-valued functions with approximate access concerns a different domain and oracle.',model_self_contained=False,requires_context=True,statement_review=dict(status='needs_specification',reviewed_on=DATE,notes=notes,remaining_issue=issue),review_note=issue,importance=dict(score=c['importance']['score'],method='editorial',reason='A fundamental adaptivity-versus-query tradeoff in distribution-free testing, with a substantial endpoint separation; exact sample accounting is necessary to state that tradeoff. Existing score retained.',assessed_on=DATE),working_summary=dict(sentences=['The tester must distinguish a k-junta from a function ε-far from all k-juntas under an unknown distribution.','The source asks for constantly many adaptive rounds and polynomially many queries in k/ε, independently of n.','Fully adaptive algorithms already have almost-linear query complexity.','The cited exponential nonadaptive lower bound charges labeled samples, while the source’s own definition counts only function queries and provides unlabeled samples.','Sample accounting and the treatment of the preliminary sample phase must be reconciled before this becomes a complete benchmark.'],basis='saved_sources',source_basis='source-text',written_on=DATE,source_refs=['primary','full','previous'])),notes=notes,checked_sources=[r['url'] for r in refs]+['https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.ICALP.2026.14'],state='improved_unfinished')
